A Nemedian priest unleashed black magic once more in the streets of Tarantia to slay men who still remained loyal to your memory. I saw it with my own eyes. Armed men dropped like flies, dying in the streets in ways no one could comprehend. And the gaunt priest laughed and said: “I am only Altaro, an acolyte of Orastes, who is but an acolyte of him who wears the veil. The power is not mine; it merely works through me.”

