Conan stared into the fire without replying. A smoldering log crashed down among the flames in a burst of sparks. It might have been the crashing ruin of his kingdom.

Again Conan felt the grim presence of reality behind the veil of illusion. He sensed once more the inexorable drive of ruthless fate. A feeling of furious panic tugged at his soul—a sense of being trapped—and a red rage that burned to destroy and kill.

